<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea buys 40,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea buys 40,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural and Fishery Marketing Corporation (AFMC) said on Wednesday it bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. No 1 soybean from Daewoo Corp at $321.22 per tonne C&amp;F and another 20,000 tonnes from Louis Dreyfus at $320.80 a tonne C&amp;F.  </p>
<p>An official at the AFMC said arrival for position one of the 20,000 tonnes was set for March 25 and the remaining 20,000 tonnes was for April 20 to the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p> POSITION TONNE	   SHIPMENT		   PRICE/SELLER</p>
<p>			U.S. Gulf	U.S. PNW	(Tonne, C&amp;F)</p>
<p>  ONE    20,000  Jan 30-Feb 18  Feb 14-Mar 5  $321.22/Daewoo</p>
<p>  TWO    20,000  Feb 24-Mar 15  Mar 11-30     $320.80/LDC</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
